    "body": "Clicking the border cell of a floating window that has a `winbar` or `'statuscolumn'` can abort\nNvim in Insert mode:\n\n    nvim: mouse.c:716: do_mouse: Assertion\n      `false && \"winbar, statusline and statuscolumn only support %@ for clicks\"` failed.\n\nLast repro I found (--clean, no plugins): float with left-only border, `winbar` and `'statuscolumn'`\nset, click the winbar row's left-border cell. In that click the translation into the float's grid\nclamps the column only on the high side, so `click_col` comes out as -1. Inside\n`do_mouse()`'s winbar/statusline/statuscolumn arm, winbar clicks are not bounds-checked at all,\nand statusline/statuscolumn clicks only check the upper bound, so we read `click_defs[-1].type`\nout of bounds. That read is the whole story: if the bytes before the array happen to be zero\n(fresh `--clean` processes) it silently does nothing, but real sessions had garbage there and a\nnon-zero `type` falls into `default:` and trips the assert. `MALLOC_PERTURB_=170` just makes that\ngarbage deterministic on glibc — it doesn't change the code path, the out-of-bounds read happens\nwith or without it. Under ASAN it fires every time, no heap luck involved:\n\n    ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow ... READ of size 4\n        #0 do_mouse src/nvim/mouse.c:730\n        #1 ins_mouse ...\n\nFix: ignore the click when `click_col < 0`, and add the missing upper bound for winbar clicks,\nmirroring how statusline clicks are already bounded. Clicks inside real `%@` regions are\nunchanged and statusline/statuscolumn behavior (including #33091) is untouched.\n\nTest added to `test/functional/ui/mouse_spec.lua`, runs under both `with ext_multigrid` and\n`without ext_multigrid`. One geometry detail so the test doesn't look magic: the float uses\n`height = 2` because with `height = 1` Nvim drops the winbar and the same click becomes a\nharmless statuscolumn click instead.\n\n    TEST_FILE=test/functional/ui/mouse_spec.lua TEST_FILTER='mouse click on floating window border' make functionaltest\n\nOn an ASAN build (`-DENABLE_ASAN_UBSAN=ON`) the test fails on master with the\nheap-buffer-overflow above and passes with this change.\n\nFixes #34110\n",
    "closed_at": null,
