            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "glepnir: right that it doesn't fail on a default build — on master the read lands on a chunk boundary that is zeroed in a fresh test child, so nothing observable happens there. what it does reproduce deterministically is the out-of-bounds read itself under an asan build (-DENABLE_ASAN_UBSAN=ON): on master the test fails with `AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow ... READ of size 4 ... mouse.c:730:37 in do_mouse` (the `click_defs[-1].type` read), and passes with the guard. the abort in the field only fires when that memory is garbage, which is the heap-state dependence (also why the crash reports are inconsistent, see MALLOC_PERTURB_ note in the PR body). trimmed the test accordingly.",
